.TH ENV-VAULT 1 "October 2026" "env-vault-cli 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
env-vault \- zero-dependency AES-256-GCM environment file encryption utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B env-vault
.I command
[\fIinput\fR] [\fIoutput\fR] [\fB\-k\fR \fIpassphrase\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B env-vault
encrypts, decrypts, rotates, and inspects local \fI.env\fR files using authenticated \fBAES-256-GCM\fR cryptography and memory-hard \fBscrypt\fR key derivation. Built strictly on native Node.js modules with zero external dependencies.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B encrypt
Encrypts a plaintext \fI.env\fR file into an authenticated \fI.env.vault\fR envelope.
.TP
.B decrypt
Verifies the authentication tag and decrypts \fI.env.vault\fR into a \fI0600\fR permissioned \fI.env\fR file.
.TP
.B rotate
Re-encrypts a vault file using a new passphrase and freshly generated salt/IV.
.TP
.B inspect
Prints non-sensitive envelope header metadata in JSON format.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ENV_VAULT_KEY
Default passphrase used when \fB\-k\fR or \fB\-\-key\fR is omitted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.TP
.B 1
CLI usage or argument error.
.TP
.B 2
Cryptographic authentication tag verification failure.
.SH AUTHOR
Abdelmalek <Abdelmalek2030github@hotmail.com>
